"rally_pxp_2026_desc", "Earn encounters with Pikachu wearing a Cosmog-themed spacesuit by completing the rally!",
"rally_pxp_2026_desc_detail", "Collect stamps by visiting GO Stamp Rally PokéStops at scenic locations around San Francisco.",
"rally_pxp_2026_location", "San Francisco, California, USA",
"rally_pxp_2026_rewards_desc", "Complete this stamp rally to earn up to six encounters with Pikachu wearing a Cosmog-themed spacesuit featuring an exclusive San Francisco Location Background.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_1", "A small but iconic Ross Alley bakery that’s been in operation since 1962.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_10", "A quirky arcade museum packed with antique coin-operated games and mechanical curiosities.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_11", "A historic chocolate-factory complex turned waterfront hangout.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_12", "A 3.5-mile Pacific-facing beach shaped by strong surf, fog, and coastal winds.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_13", "World-class modern art museum with bold architecture and major works from contemporary and 20th-century artists.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_14", "A refurbished 1898 transit terminal on the Embarcadero that now functions as a food hall and market.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_15", "San Francisco’s 1915 Beaux-Arts civic building, rebuilt after the 1906 earthquake.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_16", "The heart of SF Japantown, marked by its Peace Pagoda.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_17", "A hands-on museum for kids near Yerba Buena Gardens.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_18", "A playful waterfront photo stop designed and created by the married artist duo Claes Oldenburg and Coosje van Bruggen.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_19", "A colorful mosaic staircase featuring a delicate floral motif.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_2", "The ruins of an enormous 1890s public bathhouse built by Adolph Sutro, now a coastal leisure site.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_20", "Home to the Golden State Warriors.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_21", "A tribute to one of baseball’s greatest players and a popular gathering point outside Oracle Park.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_22", "This paddock has been home to Golden Gate Park’s resident bison herd since the 1890s.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_23", "A formal plaza created for the 1894 California Midwinter International Exposition, now neighbored by the de Young Museum and California Academy of Sciences.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_24", "A charming Golden Gate Park lakeside spot offering snacks and paddle boat rentals.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_25", "A Civil War–era brick fortress tucked beneath the Golden Gate Bridge.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_26", "A former military post turned national park.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_27", "A sandy Presidio beach with close-up bridge views.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_28", "A breezy waterfront lawn and popular picnic spot.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_29", "A 1986 sound sculpture by Peter Richards and George Gonzales that uses pipes, stone, and tidal movement to create low acoustic tones from the Bay.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_3", "An art deco tower atop Telegraph Hill.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_30", "One of the Presidio’s oldest footpaths.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_31", "The Presidio Tunnel Tops’ main lawn, built over the Doyle Drive tunnels.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_32", "A classic downtown shopping plaza and home to the San Francisco Nintendo Store!",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_33", "The ceremonial entrance to Chinatown on Grant Avenue, flanked by traditional stone lions.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_4", "A stone labyrinth near Eagle Point, accessible by coastal trail.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_5", "A 2011 Andy Goldsworthy installation in the Presidio made from eucalyptus branches laid in a winding line.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_6", "A remnant of the 1915 Panama-Pacific International Exposition, rebuilt in permanent materials after the fair.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_7", "A lively North Beach green space boasting old-school SF character.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_8", "Completed in 1972, this William Pereira–designed skyscraper is one of the most recognizable shapes in the San Francisco skyline.",
"rally_pxp_2026_stamp_description_9", "A famous row of colorful Victorian homes.",
